{
	title: 'Safe browser diagnostics and live transcript event isolation',
	spec: 'Browser and terminal transcripts only end a live turn on an explicit turn-end or non-command question event; unrelated session events (including notices and upload acknowledgements) leave the live turn and its items unchanged and cannot create a turn-end with missing status. Diagnostics are opt-in: off unless config.ason sets webDiagnostics: true. When off, the page records and sends nothing, the tab menu has no Send diagnostics action, and the host endpoint answers 404. When on, the web client initializes diagnostics before rendering, records bounded structural breadcrumbs for host event types, connection changes, visibility/resume, tab pointer/click interactions, and every character typed while focus is outside the composer: where focus was (body, dialog, field, tabs, card, button, link, other) and whether the key then reached the composer (never which key), the transcript leaving the bottom without reader input (wheel, touch, scroll keys or a scrollbar press; a running glide or a tab switch does not count), each pull back to the bottom of a pinned view (task 4s) and any pinned view left above the bottom, each also shown as a notice naming the gap and its trigger (src/web/drift.ts, a removable probe: delete the file, its line in main.tsx and the drift and pulled kinds), and reports uncaught JS errors and unhandled promise rejections. Reports contain code version, a per-page random correlation ID, timestamps, structural view/connection/viewport state (including the applied app height and whether the composer has focus) and JavaScript error name/location only: no prompt/transcript/draft text, tool inputs/results, arbitrary error messages, URLs, cookies, authentication codes or device identity. The tab menu then has a Send diagnostics action. Reports reach the host over a cookie-authenticated same-origin POST endpoint independently of the WebSocket, are validated and byte/rate bounded (a breadcrumb with a label the host does not know, as from a page newer than the host, is skipped rather than failing the report; the page drops a report the host rejected instead of resending it), and go to owner-only rotating state/web-diag.log (one 1 MiB file plus one previous file), never conversation history or tracked files. Diagnostics are best effort, must never break interactions, and use bounded memory without persistent browser storage. Tests cover unrelated live events, auth/origin/body validation, privacy filtering and bounded logging. Diagnostics do not claim to establish the historical cause of a frozen page without captured evidence. Browser controller callbacks defer circular module references until invocation so browser modules can be imported safely in any order.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The phantom end was caused by live transcript.fold falling through on attached (or another non-transcript session event), not a missing status sent by the host. Guard the ending branch, rather than hide the undefined label; the next stream must still append to the same live block. The app/tabs cycle also had an eager tabs.backgroundStep reference; a lazy callback fixes import-order failures.',
		'Reports are structural and project away unknown fields on the host. Actual body reads are capped at 16 KiB, 32 breadcrumbs per report, 30 accepted attempts per host minute, and client sends at most every five seconds; failed sends retain only the latest 32 entries for a future interaction/resume. Real Chromium mobile smoke exercised tab navigation, manual reporting, uncaught TypeError and rejected RangeError while ensuring their private messages never reached the log. A browser whose main thread is entirely blocked cannot report until it resumes; telemetry is evidence, not proof all freezes are fixed.',
		'Task 6cm/m7 evidence needs: the key breadcrumb (composer|other) says whether outside typing reached the box; context appHeight against viewportHeight/height separates a stale visual viewport from stale CSS, and composerFocused separates a focused composer without keyboard from an unfocused one. Before the host skipped unknown labels, one new kind failed the whole report and the page resent it forever; the client now drops 400s. A host only learns new labels on restart, while the page rebuilds from source at once.',
		'Diagnostics were on for every user until the user ruled diagnostics and telemetry opt-in (AGENTS.md Privacy). The key breadcrumb listens in capture phase on window, so a handler that stops the event cannot hide it; the old record in Chat.tsx missed keys while focus sat in a field or dialog.',
		'The drift probe compares against its own record of reader input, not scroll.ts state, so it stays removable in one file. In headless Chrome, Page.setWebLifecycleState frozen never resumes animation frames, so it cannot model a background tab; switching to a second target with Target.activateTarget does (frames pause while hidden and resume).'
	],
	needs: ['w5', '8a']
}
